<main class="content">
<section class="policy" id="overview"><h2>01. Overview and scope</h2>
<p>Stratic Market is a marketplace that helps independent sellers publish product listings and helps customers discover products, contact sellers, place orders and arrange payment. The service also includes account features, chat, seller dashboards and parcel-related information pages.</p>
<p>This notice describes the information processed through the Stratic Market application and website. It is intended to be read together with the <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>. It is not a promise that a website, network, storage provider or device can never fail. No online service can guarantee uninterrupted availability or zero risk of data loss.</p>
<p>By using a feature, you should provide only information that is relevant to that feature. Do not upload passwords, one-time passcodes, bank PINs, full card details or other secrets into product descriptions, chat messages, photos or support requests.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="data"><h2>02. Information that may be collected</h2>
<h3>Account and identity information</h3><p>Depending on the sign-in method and the information you provide, the service may process your name, email address, mobile number, account identifier, country, language preference and authentication-related records. Passwords are stored as password hashes rather than as readable passwords.</p>
<h3>Seller and product information</h3><p>When a seller creates or edits a listing, the service processes the product title, description, category, price, reference price, shop name, seller contact details, location or address details supplied for the listing, product images, optional additional images, and an optional seller payment QR image. Listing identifiers and creation or edit timestamps are also used to manage the catalogue.</p>
<h3>Buyer, order and delivery information</h3><p>When a customer places an order, the service may process the customer's name, phone number, delivery address, city, country, postal code, selected payment method, order contents, quantities, totals, transaction reference supplied by the customer, seller details and order status. Parcel request features may process sender and receiver contact and address details, parcel description, weight, dimensions, declared value and carrier references where supplied.</p>
<h3>Chat, support and usage information</h3><p>Chat messages, message timestamps, delivery and read status, message edits or deletion status, and images shared in chat may be stored to provide conversations. The service may also process product views, likes, basic device or session identifiers, error and security events, and activity needed to operate dashboards and prevent abuse.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="use"><h2>03. How information is used</h2><ul>
<li>To create and authenticate accounts and maintain sign-in sessions.</li><li>To publish, display, search, update and manage product listings.</li><li>To connect a buyer with the seller of the particular product being viewed or purchased.</li><li>To create orders, display order status and support seller-buyer communication.</li><li>To show product views, likes, sales summaries and other seller dashboard information.</li><li>To display the payment method configured for the specific seller and product.</li><li>To provide chat delivery, read receipts, message editing and deletion features.</li><li>To maintain service security, investigate suspected fraud, enforce the Terms of Use and diagnose technical failures.</li><li>To respond to support requests and comply with applicable legal obligations.</li></ul>
<p>Information should not be used for a purpose unrelated to operating, securing or supporting the feature through which it was provided, except where permitted or required by law.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="sharing"><h2>04. When information is shared</h2>
<p>Marketplace activity requires limited information to be visible to the people involved. A public product listing can display its title, description, price, product photographs and seller/shop information intended for customers. A seller receives the buyer and order information needed to fulfil an order. A buyer can see the seller information and payment option associated with the selected product.</p>
<p>Information may be processed by infrastructure and service providers that host the application, database, uploaded media or payment flow. For example, the application is designed to use PostgreSQL-compatible database storage and may use Get Pronto for product image delivery when configured. Gateway payments use the payment provider selected by the seller, such as Razorpay. Those providers process information under their own terms and privacy notices.</p>
<p>Information may also be disclosed when required by law, to respond to valid legal process, to protect users or the service from harm, or in connection with a legitimate business reorganisation. Stratic Market does not offer personal information for sale as a data-broker product.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="payments"><h2>05. Seller payment QR codes, gateways and secrets</h2>
<p>A seller's uploaded QR image is associated with that seller's individual product record. When a buyer chooses the QR payment option for that product, the application requests the QR associated with that exact product. The intended design is not to use a shared global QR for all sellers. A buyer should always verify the payee name and amount in their payment application before approving a transfer.</p>
<p>If a seller connects a supported payment gateway, the server uses the seller's gateway credentials to create and verify payment transactions. The secret credential is encrypted before it is stored and is not intended to be returned to the buyer's browser. The public Key ID may be used by the payment checkout. Keep gateway credentials private and rotate them through the provider if they may have been exposed.</p>
<div class="callout"><b>Important security notice:</b> Encryption depends on the server's configured encryption key remaining available and protected. The operator must keep the production encryption key stable, private and backed up securely. If that key is lost or changed without a migration, previously encrypted credentials may no longer be decryptable. Never place a live secret key in a screenshot, chat, source-code repository or public issue.</div>
<p>Stratic Market is not a bank and does not hold customer funds in a wallet. QR payments are made through the payment application chosen by the customer. A transaction reference entered by a buyer is not, by itself, proof that the payment has settled. Sellers should verify payment in their own bank or payment-provider account before dispatching goods.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="media"><h2>06. Product photographs, QR images and other media</h2>
<p>Product photographs and additional listing images are used to display the seller's products. A payment QR is stored separately by product and is served through a private, authenticated payment endpoint rather than the public product-image route. Chat photographs are accessible only to participants in the relevant conversation through the authenticated chat image route.</p>
<p>Media may be stored in application storage and database-backed storage, with an optional external image provider for delivery. Availability can still be affected by provider outages, configuration errors, account limits, accidental deletion, corrupted uploads or infrastructure failure. Sellers should retain original copies of important photographs and QR images outside the application.</p>
<p>Do not upload an image unless you have the right to use it and it does not contain information that should remain private. Avoid uploading identity documents, bank statements, payment card images or unrelated personal photographs.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="chat"><h2>07. Chat messages and deletion controls</h2>
<p>Chat is designed for communication between the buyer and seller associated with a product conversation. Message status may indicate whether a message was sent, delivered or read. Message content and images may be stored so the conversation can be loaded across sessions and devices.</p>
<p>When a participant deletes one of their own live messages for everyone, the content is replaced with a deleted-message notice in the conversation. Removing that notice from your own view is a separate action and should not remove the other participant's notice. A participant may also select multiple eligible messages and apply the available deletion action.</p>
<p>Deletion from the application does not necessarily remove copies that another person has already saved, photographed, exported or received through device notifications. Operational backups and database replicas may also retain data for a limited period according to the storage system's lifecycle. Do not send information in chat that you would not want the other participant to retain.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="storage"><h2>08. Storage, security and reliability</h2>
<p>The application uses server-side access controls for account-specific features, private payment QR retrieval and chat media. Database queries and payment verification are performed by the server. Passwords are hashed, and supported gateway secrets are encrypted before storage. These controls reduce risk but cannot make any internet service completely secure.</p>
<p>Production deployments must use durable managed database storage and correctly configured persistent or object storage for media. Temporary application filesystems can be erased during a restart or redeployment. Database credentials, API keys, encryption keys and provider access tokens must be kept in private deployment environment settings and must never be committed to a public repository.</p>
<p>Access to personal information should be limited to people and service providers who need it to operate, maintain, secure or support the service. The operator should review access permissions, backups, provider settings and security logs regularly.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="retention"><h2>09. Data retention</h2>
<p>Information is retained for as long as it is reasonably needed to provide the relevant feature, maintain account and transaction records, resolve disputes, protect the service, or meet legal requirements. Product listings may have an expiry date that affects whether they are displayed in the active catalogue; expiry is not the same as a promise that the underlying record or media is automatically erased.</p>
<p>Chat, order, payment and security records may be retained for operational or legal reasons. When information is no longer required, it should be deleted or de-identified using the relevant administrative process, subject to backup cycles and legal requirements. Retention periods may differ by record type and infrastructure provider.</p>
<p>Users should not assume that information will be stored forever or that a backup can be restored in every failure scenario. Keep independent copies of important business records, product photographs, QR images and gateway recovery information.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="choices"><h2>10. Your choices and responsibilities</h2><ul>
<li>Keep account contact details accurate and use a strong, unique password.</li><li>Only upload product images and payment QR codes that belong to the relevant seller and listing.</li><li>Use the product editing and account features to correct information that you control.</li><li>Use the chat controls to delete eligible messages and remove deleted-message notices from your own view.</li><li>Contact support for help with an account, privacy concern, suspected security issue or incorrect listing.</li><li>Do not share OTPs, passwords, gateway secrets, bank PINs or recovery codes with anyone.</li></ul>
<p>Requests to access, correct or delete information may need identity verification so that another person's account or records are not changed by mistake. Some records may need to be retained where required by law or to resolve an existing transaction or dispute.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="cookies"><h2>11. Cookies, sessions and device information</h2>
<p>The application may use session cookies or similar browser storage to keep a user signed in, protect requests and remember limited preferences. A device or browser identifier may be used to count visits or product views and to support service integrity. Browser settings can restrict cookies, but doing so may prevent sign-in or other features from working correctly.</p>
<p>Basic technical information such as browser requests, timestamps, network information and error details may be processed by the hosting environment for security, diagnostics and reliability. The exact information available depends on the browser, hosting provider and deployment configuration.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="children"><h2>12. Children and supervised use</h2>
<p>Stratic Market is a commercial marketplace and is not designed as a children's social network. Anyone who is not legally able to enter into a purchase, sale or other agreement in their location should use the service only with the involvement and permission of a parent or legal guardian where required. Do not submit another person's personal information without appropriate authority.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="changes"><h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>This policy may be revised when application features, infrastructure providers, payment integrations or legal requirements change. The effective date at the top identifies the current published version. Material changes should be reflected on this page. Continued use after a change is subject to the revised notice to the extent permitted by applicable law.</p>
<p>Check this page periodically, especially before uploading new categories of information or enabling a new payment or delivery feature.</p></section>
<section class="policy" id="contact"><h2>14. Contact, product and service links</h2>
<p>For help with an account, listing, order, privacy concern or suspected security issue, open the application help area and provide only the minimum information needed to identify the issue. Do not include passwords, OTPs, full payment credentials or gateway secrets in a support request.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/shop">Open Stratic Market</a> — browse products, access your profile and shop tools.</li>
<li><a href="/shop#sell-form">Open the product upload form</a> — create or update a product listing.</li>
<li><a href="/book-parcel">Open parcel booking</a> — submit a parcel service request.</li>
<li><a href="/track">Track a parcel request</a> — look up a request using its reference and phone number.</li>
<li><a href="/help">Visit the Help Centre</a> — read service guidance and safety information.</li>
<li><a href="/terms">Read the Terms of Use</a> — review the rules for using the service.</li>
</ul>
<p class="small">This notice is a product privacy explanation, not legal advice. The service operator should have this document reviewed for the countries in which the marketplace operates and should add a verified legal contact channel before relying on it as a complete statutory privacy notice.</p></section>
